    "notes": "The target-machine Windows RTX4090 editor-paint closeout for 20260523-r58 passed validation, attribution, artifact verification, and closeout. The verified owner decision is owner=canvas-paint-replay, action=open-canvas-paint-replay-slice, with paint.widget / Canvas as the dominant attribution owner. The first follow-on editor-canvas-paint-replay-slice-v1 is closed after r59. The second follow-on editor-canvas-paint-replay-plan-cache-v1 is closed after r61 as a baseline-neutral overlapping-window replay-plan cache improvement; r61 still selected owner=canvas-paint-replay, and complex-wheel/preedit-heavy frames reported no plan-cache hits. The third follow-on editor-canvas-paint-replay-preedit-plan-cache-v1 is closed after r62; it restored partial replay-plan cache reuse for non-preedit rows and moved complex-wheel from plan_cache_hits=0/candidates=10115/probe=2800us/key_compare=323us to plan_cache_hits=10041/candidates=74/probe=7us/key_compare=0us. The parent owner still remains canvas-paint-replay, so the next bounded slice should target remaining Canvas replay/touch/row-paint overhead rather than row-scene prepaint planning. Do not reopen closed historical Canvas attribution lanes unless fresh evidence explicitly makes them the right scope. Local independent optimization slices may continue when they have their own evidence, but they must not drive checked-in baseline changes unless the Windows RTX4090 artifacts justify it. Split narrow follow-ons only for the remaining Canvas replay owner, implementation-heavy rewrites, Linux profile adoption, or code-editor feature closure when the audit or contract matrix identifies a concrete hotspot or missing environment profile. Do not mark the broader performance goal complete while ui-perf-contract-audit.md still says the goal is active or while Linux and other environment-specific baselines remain missing."
